#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115075 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "51a437bf-2a11-5eba-a046-4770d41214ca" :question/math-academy-id "e-4720" :question/problem "Let ![](images/a9/a9f425a48a3ed8fabfce0eb1785ebdddc62d7dd3208ac302fd66a89b03e58cdb.svg) Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=5{R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation $R_2:=5R_1+ R_2$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115076 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/id #uuid "9927d1a6-a119-5987-9f49-5171a3f2e2d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4721" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/11/11c345fde8fecb2e2a5459a0868ad8892e9067820de72f91601c1033858ca019.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "0f08f8aa-63e3-500a-987e-e9888b9b0479" :question/math-academy-id "e-4722" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2, \\qquad  R_2:=R_2+3R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/ea/ead4157a19d725334c44a55903b52bd12d7627e73696c2100efee52340347468.svg)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](images/ba/ba70270430d6c5606e816c16c606c8f3940742a48c95b0ad8a33f6c935da8cf6.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436813 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "041b2509-a556-5b7c-ab45-9ca5fd9c3cc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-15{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436753} {:answer/id #uuid "08e24a6d-b6f5-53e0-a5c7-349a5368a361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=15{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436757} {:answer/id #uuid "6c046924-1709-5274-a794-1f3b95605dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=15{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436775} {:answer/id #uuid "7e45231b-e9d5-5367-ad87-33c31af8b88a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-15{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436779} {:answer/id #uuid "7f2d5e69-ef35-54de-a461-09d176c29c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-15{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f2d5e69-ef35-54de-a461-09d176c29c43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-15{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436780} :answer-field/id #uuid "3095f9c5-6e39-53cb-accf-8b0a4693c3a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0469c521-df52-516d-97d5-643098592b19" :question/math-academy-id "q-130841" :question/problem "Let  $E=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the first row of the identity matrix  by $-15$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-15{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:=-15{R}_{1}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21333662-4221-5556-87c3-a82bacc85a82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=(-6){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436762} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0aec34-380f-59c7-b0b9-bab7ff9c5edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+6{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436763} {:answer/id #uuid "40cb2605-d7af-5bce-abf6-276350c8dc19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436765} {:answer/id #uuid "bf2a402f-3c31-5995-88ca-f0b9c765a7e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-6){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436791} {:answer/id #uuid "e0355739-0916-506f-b796-ffbe20c9beba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=(-6){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40cb2605-d7af-5bce-abf6-276350c8dc19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436765} :answer-field/id #uuid "0be5a703-ade8-5f32-9eae-8fc699a6f178" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88681796-21e9-5e72-a195-e1da66276721" :question/math-academy-id "q-130842" :question/problem "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of the identity matrix and adding $-6$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-6){R}_{1}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "090417bb-bda0-5586-94b2-46eceb1bcbb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -16 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263085} {:answer/id #uuid "1a096cdf-7202-57cc-a632-c055625d37b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263249} {:answer/id #uuid "7da1c9d4-e363-5fed-ba08-cd3350bed811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 16 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264083} {:answer/id #uuid "e47515dc-5670-5487-907c-2b04a5fa6d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264988} {:answer/id #uuid "e7e39e79-758a-5180-b1de-9ef5ce975ce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e47515dc-5670-5487-907c-2b04a5fa6d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264988} :answer-field/id #uuid "e20c3493-b518-5f90-8021-6c1e33bc6aff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265645}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7993ea70-2f40-5504-828e-aeb8566a66bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130847" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+16{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+16{R}_{1}$ to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+16{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 16 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f389b7a-bb36-5074-8c96-fb1ecf9fa6df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263288} {:answer/id #uuid "8241a5d7-02a1-547d-baef-267aa901fd37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264119} {:answer/id #uuid "84a7fac4-e47e-5983-a206-08e59164fb7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264139} {:answer/id #uuid "b1263628-59c7-546e-a4af-aac116f01421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264525} {:answer/id #uuid "c5653eec-b4a3-5077-bd82-07173a4abb55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1263628-59c7-546e-a4af-aac116f01421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264525} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd48ee5b-7dbe-500d-a87b-ee2f033ad6d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "837dfba2-f78f-5c76-b27f-bb2d2c133624" :question/math-academy-id "q-130860" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265997 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200326c6-4e9b-5f9d-8ea8-3c7fd8caa616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263292} {:answer/id #uuid "783d2411-8439-515d-972b-2e98645d0bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264043} {:answer/id #uuid "94702e89-66e6-5edd-9c50-630d134703e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264271} {:answer/id #uuid "96a95a1d-d7ee-55e3-9d5d-b9c01aab924a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264289} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a3316a-6a18-572b-8fbd-42d9ba63f793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94702e89-66e6-5edd-9c50-630d134703e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264271} :answer-field/id #uuid "97f26578-678b-584b-94d3-3bf45adddf76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a5d6a7d0-f153-5a48-8ab8-2274611f50fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130862" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the three given elementary row operations. \n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2034d0-7cda-5f39-9589-90aba5659d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436758} {:answer/id #uuid "49fe98f4-4ffc-5af2-83a4-d3f36bfa74f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436770} {:answer/id #uuid "4d910c4e-a0ac-50d5-9159-50d27df48002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436771} {:answer/id #uuid "7a31368e-5bda-5127-82e3-a85cb11c6a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436778} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6c5718-69bf-54af-9c04-7a6648adfb74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49fe98f4-4ffc-5af2-83a4-d3f36bfa74f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436770} :answer-field/id #uuid "98133f54-d0b4-500e-be6b-d23f4be79f09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "338846a1-5093-5e28-a69f-a5c5dede7770" :question/math-academy-id "q-130863" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{1}=7{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}={R}_{1}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}=7{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}=7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e96febe-54c3-5e3a-a3b3-7bd0082d0748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436764} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1ac934-f42e-5421-a48c-557b71cea666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436784} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7860a0-b9d2-5afc-af0b-2703b7594661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436787} {:answer/id #uuid "f2338944-0fa0-5908-a315-427b16f9b9fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436799} {:answer/id #uuid "f88a4afc-f340-5d8a-8f8b-7f4abe4ed444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2338944-0fa0-5908-a315-427b16f9b9fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436799} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef5c36a4-d082-5926-820f-4cd3513e1032" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "535f214d-c021-5eea-9acd-b13d4504df24" :question/math-academy-id "q-31977" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row  operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115246 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07e35b25-669e-55d1-afe7-e324171bb24a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-5){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436755} {:answer/id #uuid "7fd22bfe-ec1d-572b-acb0-a9341c95ca1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436781} {:answer/id #uuid "94c48f90-9bd5-5d16-a188-2cca931f231d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=5{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436783} {:answer/id #uuid "d191fc7a-1435-519a-aadd-42c211b37297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436793} {:answer/id #uuid "f65184d9-bfa6-542f-9d5c-645cc46c8862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f65184d9-bfa6-542f-9d5c-645cc46c8862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436800} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ea2baf5-4b46-568a-a3d6-feb9ec4d750b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b4493b8f-a3b6-5d7e-9641-4ac3f05dd564" :question/math-academy-id "q-42759" :question/problem "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the first row of the identity matrix and adding $5$ times the second row: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115248 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fi