:question/math-academy-id "q-75087" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}$ to $A.$  \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436821 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115247 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08df48ed-79af-5bf2-85ef-d1439433ab47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436756} {:answer/id #uuid "0f089b50-55e5-516b-9f45-db7bc3a03d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436759} {:answer/id #uuid "487debef-ed20-58c1-b2bb-36f8c9abf586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436769} {:answer/id #uuid "6e60ea78-a600-5e26-8bc9-6dc62c40ffde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436776} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d1e1c7-900d-5649-b458-08e60264afaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1d1e1c7-900d-5649-b458-08e60264afaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436785} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bba64a8-5bb2-5bab-90e3-aa7ac4488ef1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc406c3a-4f36-5f35-99c4-51a064b8434e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75088" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-12{R}_{2}\\,$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-12{R}_{2}$  to $A.$ \n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-12{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}]}
